      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Automated Testing Phase Security Gates:\n\n1. Static Application Security Testing (SAST): Utilize tools like SonarQube or Checkmarx to analyze source code for potential vulnerabilities and code quality issues.\n\n2. Dynamic Application Security Testing (DAST): Implement tools such as OWASP ZAP or Burp Suite to perform active scanning of running applications for security weaknesses.\n\n3. Dependency Scanning: Use tools like OWASP Dependency-Check or Snyk to identify known vulnerabilities in third-party libraries and dependencies.\n\n4. Container Scanning: Employ tools like Clair or Trivy to scan container images for security vulnerabilities.\n\nStaging Phase Security Gates:\n\n1. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Scanning: Integrate tools like Terraform or AWS CloudFormation with security scanning tools to detect misconfigurations in infrastructure code.\n\n2. Configuration Management: Use tools like Ansible or Puppet to enforce secure configurations and prevent unauthorized changes.\n\n3. Network Segmentation: Implement network segmentation and access controls to limit the exposure of staging environments to external networks.\n\n4. Continuous Monitoring: Deploy tools like Prometheus or Nagios for real-time monitoring of the staging environment to detect and respond to security incidents.\n\nAutomated Scanning Tools:\n\n1. SonarQube\n2",
